From 461b0a44d1273c3b187678e5a6f7f798fc5a23b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Rowlinson <mrowlinson@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:16:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/23] avcodec/ac4: emit DSI extradata via putbits serializer

Vendor the DSI serializer from the parent dsi/ lib
(ff/dsi-lavcshape-merged, DSI-11/DSI-12) into libavcodec and adopt
the PutBitContext emitter for codec extradata in the native AC-4
encoder wrapper.

Vendored, PutBitContext emission only (the hand-rolled oracle
ac4dsi_serialize and the legacy layout-name shim stay parent-side):
ac4dsi.h, ac4dsi_priv.h, ac4dsi_putbits.h/.c, ac4dsi.c (init
helpers, lavc-mask layout table, shared validation). Integer-only:
wired under CONFIG_AC4_ENCODER without the CFLAGS-ac4enc_float list.

The wrapper builds one raw ac4_dsi_v1 payload at init (no atom
header; the MP4 muxer wraps it verbatim as dac4): lib-default
stream params plus the snapped target bitrate, one synthesized pv1
presentation, channel trio set explicitly for the validated
stereo/5.1 layout (mask-table form follows). Any serializer refusal
fails init loudly; DSI can never be silently missing.

Encoder packet bytes are unchanged (fate md5 REFs untouched, .ac4
cmp-clean); the three framecrc refs gain the #extradata line the
framecrc muxer now prints (size 32, oracle-verified bytes).

Re-cut (r3): content rebased onto the r3 stack (fuzz-guarded
wrapper + re-pinned stereo refs); DSI bytes and #extradata
checksums identical to r2-wire.

Signed-off-by: Michael Rowlinson <mrowlinson@gmail.com>
